      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fdb23bd4-f894-5e01-b68f-2425fa7fb607",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aleksandras Stulginskis, Kazys Grinius, Antanas Smetona, Vytautas Petrulis, Kazys Jokantas\n- Organizations: Farmers' Association\n- Roles: President of Lithuania, acting President of Lithuania\n- Events: 1926 military coup in Lithuania\n\nFacts:\n- Kazys Grinius was born on 17 December 1866 and died on 4 June 1950.\n- Kazys Grinius was the third President of Lithuania and served from 7 June 1926 to 17 December 1926.\n- In 1926, a military coup in Lithuania was led by Antanas Smetona and brought down President Kazys Grinius.\n- Later in 1926, Aleksandras Stulginskis served as acting President of Lithuania for a few hours after the military coup.\n- The Farmers' Association was led by Aleksandras Stulginskis, Vytautas Petrulis, and Kazys Jokantas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2418ff9d-fa49-5a6b-baed-c0992a19b906",
        "text": "Page: Aleksandras Stulginskis. Sentence: Stulginskis was also acting President of Lithuania for a few hours later in 1926, following a military coup that was led by his predecessor as President (Antanas Smetona) and which had brought down Stulginskis's successor, Kazys Grinius.\nPage: Kazys Grinius. Sentence: Kazys Grinius (] , 17 December 18664 June 1950) was the third President of Lithuania, and held that office from 7 June 1926 to 17 December 1926.\nPage: Farmers' Association. Sentence: Its leaders included Aleksandras Stulginskis, Vytautas Petrulis and Kazys Jokantas.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
